# Docs describe this project only

A client repo is a standalone product. README, AGENTS.md, product docs, coding guides, and comments must make sense to a developer who does not know the studio process or any other stack.

## Write

- What this project is, what it uses, and how to work in it.
- The stack in the positive: name the tools that are here.

## Do not write

- Tools this project does not use, including “do not add X” lists.
- The studio, the template, workshop phases, or a “what this repo is not” section.
- Banners, caveats, or completeness asides that only make sense from an earlier chat.

## Example

Bad: Do not add Supabase, Refine, or TanStack Query. Convex queries and mutations are the data layer.

Good: Convex queries and mutations are the data layer. Zustand is only for client extras.

This rule does not apply when editing studio factory files under `project-template/docs/client-delivery/` or `project-template/docs/new-project-scaffold.md`. Those files may say what to copy and what to omit.
